//RS //! The parser only records the raw shape it saw (`EveryArg` — a duration
//RS //! literal or a quoted string) and, at parse time, whether `#Every(…)` is
//RS //! paired with `#Job` on the same function (E0925, pushed directly by
//RS //! `jet-parser` — a placement question, not a value question). This module
//RS //! owns the one thing left for schedules: is the VALUE a real schedule?
//RS //! This module resolves the raw marker through the registered unit-plane
//RS //! facts and writes one checked `EverySchedule` projection onto the marker.
//RS //! Runtime consumers read that projection; they never parse source suffixes.
//RS //!
//RS //! D-JOB-NAMES1=A also lives here: a `#Job fn` must not take a reserved name,
//RS //! `run`/`dev`/`build`/`test`/`help`/`version` (E0928).
//RS //!
//RS //! I3: this module only decides; codegen never reads `Func::every` at all —
//RS //! a `#Job`/`#Every` function generates as an ordinary fn.
